t A nonreproducible artifact satisfies a reproducible release/signing gate or a reproducibility claim lacks its recipe. Emit Nonreproducibility exception and release decision; PKG7001/PKG7008. Dependencies: PKG7, PKG12. Criterion behavior/pkg7/recorded-build-recipe: accept Emit a schema-valid release build recipe binding package/version, source/project/lock/compiler/toolchain, graph/task settings, concrete profile/target matrix, controlled environment/locale/timezone/traversal/timestamps/seeds/network, generator/input hashes, blobs/FFI inputs, expected artifact identities, output hashes and verification command or machine-readable equivalent. Rebuild twice under that exact recipe and compare canonical manifests and actual content hashes. For standard-library packages retain source commit, build graph, compiler, package lock, tests and policy-required signatures in the provenance record. Reject Reject a claimed reproducible release with no recipe, omitted or altered consumed inputs/outputs, unlocked dependencies, unrecorded network/randomness, host path leakage, missing generator hashes, filename-only comparison or unexplained hash drift; mark uncontrolled inputs nonreproducible and deny reproducible signing/release claims when policy requires reproducibility. Standard-library provenance and artifact identity must agree; neither API inventory nor a supplied success label proves a rebuild. Emit Versioned build-recipe artifact, controlled-environment manifest, input/output digest lists, actual repeat-build canonical comparison, exception list and PKG7001-PKG7008 diagnostics with recipe/input/artifact/target/environment context; standard-library source/build/lock/test/signature provenance links. Dependencies: PKG1/PKG2 project, lock and typed graph producers, PKG3 canonical manifests, PKG5 complete dependency lock, PKG10/PKG12 provenance/signing evidence, stdlib/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/integrate-platform-modules-and-close-release-manifests module/package manifests,