     :role :runtime-audit-producer,
     :criterion-text
     "Denial at actual service hook, redacted diagnostics and source-map preservation. R1/R11/R12: every authority-bearing action carries principal/package/deployment/artifact/source/effect/capability identity; deny by default and check both caller grant and tool/plugin contract; delegated handles are typed, scoped, provider-bound and revocable where supported, with use-after-revocation rejection; preserve grant/deny/delegate/revoke/audit records without secret disclosure and enforce deployment narrowing. Structured event/log/trace/metric/panic/replay bundles retain stable schemas/IDs, runtime/profile/target/source/generated-origin/artifact links, check/proof/replay references, redaction and remediation; sinks require grants, development services are marked, and sampling retains mandatory audit events without changing ordering, replay or safety. Reject ambient authority, ungranted sinks, secret/tainted/raw-memory leakage and lost required mappings/events. Dependencies: Auth supplies policy and grants, Lower supplies artifact/source maps, each runtime family supplies events, and testing/tooling/incident consumers validate bundles; these records do not grant authority or claim execution acceptance. P4: map actual lowered/generated host failures to Gravity source and generated origins where supported or required; record unavailable mappings honestly and reject missing required mappings. Compiler diagnostic emission alone is not this runtime consumer evidence. Criterion profile-gap/hosted/failure-source-mapping (Open): Input: Actual hosted runtime failure and emitted source/generated-origin mappings for the claimed runtime/version/host symbol and lowered artifact. Accept: Resolve the failure to Gravity source and generated-origin chains where supported or required; explicitly report unavailable mappings where conditional support permits. Reject: Missing required mapping, incorrect generated-origin chain and compiler diagnostic emission substituted for actual host-failure mapping evidence. Required outputs: Runtime source/diagnostic map and executed source-mapping fixture, P4-SOURCEMAP diagnostic with runtime/symbol/origin/policy context; unsupported optional mapping is recorded honestly. Dependencies: runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-memory-concurrency-and-typed-ffi-boundaries, diag/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/preserve-primaryrelatedgenerated-origins-and-stable-order, emit/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/emit3-bind-provenance-to-bytes interface facts, not whole-task completion. Exact source predicates and frozen evidence: specs/requirement-reconciliation/profile-system/gap-completion.edn, mapping hosted/failure-source-mapping; all attached contextual and negative predicates remain required. No implementation acceptance is inferred. Criterion behavior/pkg6/runtime-permission-audit: accept For participating runtimes, record requested/granted/denied/used permission events with package/effect/capability/profile/target, grant source and policy identity in the declared audit schema. Reject A required use/denial event is missing, a runtime effect has no capability derivation or audit output discloses protected authority data. Emit Runtime permission audit records/schema linked to capability manifest and SBOM, with PKG6002 context for missing derivation. Dependencies: PKG6, R11, R12.",
