     :criterion-text
     "No externally visible operation after denial; explicit grant provenance end to end. For SAFE10/SAFE13/SAFE14, execute service-boundary allowed/denied fixtures with provider presence/scope, typed error or declared panic and required audit/telemetry; redact secrets. Tool schema checks, side-effect class and human-review policy must precede invocation; package/build authority cannot silently become runtime grants. A compiler authorization record alone is insufficient runtime enforcement evidence. Criterion behavior/pkg6/request-grant-separation: accept Deploy only scoped handles for capabilities requested by the package and allowed by deployment policy; keep source requests, package requests, denials and actual grants distinct. Reject A dependency grants authority, a deployment grants an unrequested capability, or a runtime effect uses ambient authority instead of its scoped handle. Emit Package-to-deployment grant/handle provenance and PKG6005/PKG6006 before the effect. Dependencies: L15, SAFE10, PKG6, R11. Criterion behavior/pkg6/transitive-deny-precedence: accept Check every source-analysis/project/manifest/resolver/deployment/runtime edge; explicit denials remain effective across transitive dependency requests. Reject Any required edge is missing, a transitive request overrides denial, or an action/build proceeds despite conflicting policy. Emit Authority-chain decision with dependency chain/effect/capability/grant source/policy and PKG6004. Dependencies: PKG6, PKG5, SAFE10, R11.",
